# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even though this repo lives on Windows.
# A .sh checked out with CRLF fails on Linux before it runs a single line --
# the kernel reads the shebang as "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and reports
# "bad interpreter: no such file or directory", which points at bash rather
# than at the line endings and is a genuinely confusing hour to lose.
*.sh text eol=lf
